From 4fd668ef89f936da6b874de7e9a8302e9838ce6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
Date: Tue, 21 May 2024 09:45:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/45] drivers: adc: microchip: Add ADC driver for MEC5 HAL
 based chips

Add an ADC driver for the multi-channel SAR based ADC in the
Microchip MEC5 HAL based chips: MEC174x, MEC175x, and MECH172x.
Driver supports PM and device PM. Note: PM support makes use of
a PM API to block suspend to RAM. This API can only lock one PM
state per call. If more low power states must be blocked or the
application changes suspend to RAM to standby or another deep
sleep equivalent state the driver will not block those. The driver
would need a build time list of deep sleep states to know which
one(s) to block. Device PM is preferrable.

Signed-off-by: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
---
