From 0e03669be38b7326163656804adf6f8b5f352b0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
Date: Tue, 21 May 2024 11:02:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/45] drivers: espi: microchip: New eSPI driver architecture
 for MEC5 HAL

Add a new architecture eSPI driver for Microchip MEC5 HAL based chips.
ESPI OOB and flash channel are split out into separate files in a
MCHP specific subfolder. Peripheral channels devices are split out
into separate sub-drivers allowing new sub-drivers with different
customer requirements to be used for each peripheral. ESPI device
tree has also bee re-architecture moving peripheral device features
to be specified in DT. Virtual wires are also fully specified by DT.
Driver tables for peripheral channel devices and VWires are generated
by DT macros instead of being hard coded. Note: DTSI files are in a
separate commit.

Signed-off-by: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
