From c61738802c48a2d4edb40bc94f02c6bdd26afe0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Jun 2024 14:55:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/45] drivers: espi: microchip: MEC5 generic ACPI EC driver

WIP (Work in Progress)
Add a generic ACPI EC driver that passes processing commands/data
send by the host to the application. The driver reads command/data
from the hardware and clears input buffer full interrupt before
invoking application callback. Driver will support an API to enable
and disable its IBF and OBE interrupts. This is a sub-driver of
MEC5 eSPI and implements an API the core eSPI driver uses when
the platform reset virtual wire de-asserts indicating the host
will have access to eSPI peripheral channel devices.

Signed-off-by: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
---
