From e33a8c942f01af1b1d6986a4b40e53e7d52a6c14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Jun 2024 12:51:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/45] drivers: watchdog: microchip: mec5: Add MEC5 HAL based
 WDT driver

Watch dog timer driver for Microchip MEC5 SoC's. The WDT in these
parts is a 16-bit down counter decrementing at 1.007 ms. This WDT
is on the 32 KHz clock domain and can operation in deep sleep. It
has two modes of operation: reset or interrupt. In interrupt mode
the WDT will fire an interrupt when its counter reaches 0, disable
its interrupt enable, and reload the counter from the load register.
The driver does implement WDT multistage support but this has not
been tested.

Signed-off-by: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
