From befde3a012b48cda18b717cb54ae3a9476600bfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Jun 2024 20:39:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/45] drivers: i2c: microchip: MEC5 HAL based I2C driver
 using network layer

Initial I2C driver for MEC5 HAL based Microchip SoC making use of the
I2C network layer hardware FSM's and DMA. Network layer was designed
for complete I2C transactions from START to STOP. This driver is limited
to one message I2C write, one messge I2C read, or two messages I2C write
followed by I2C read. The NL FSM hardware also limits message write and
read byte counts to 65535 bytes but this must also include the target
addresses and optional PEC bytes. The driver limits write and read
message lengths to 65532 bytes. The uses two DMA channels via the Zephyr
DMA driver. Initial driver implementation supports controller mode only.
The hardware support targets mode with two matching addresses.

Signed-off-by: Scott Worley <scott.worley@microchip.com>
